# SPA fallback for Netlify / Cloudflare Pages.
#
# NOTE: production actually runs on CloudPanel/nginx (see DEPLOYMENT.md), so
# nginx never reads this file — the equivalent `try_files` rule is configured
# directly in the CloudPanel vhost. This file is kept for portability, in
# case the site is ever mirrored to Netlify/Cloudflare Pages.
#
# Every unknown path must serve index.html so the client router can handle it —
# without this, a hard refresh on /merchants returns a real 404.
#
# The 200 status is what makes it a rewrite rather than a redirect (the URL in
# the address bar is preserved). The trade-off: genuinely unknown paths also
# return 200, which is why NotFoundPage sets `noIndex` — see
# src/features/errors/NotFoundPage.tsx.
#
# On other hosts the equivalent is:
#   nginx    → try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html;   (this is what CloudPanel uses)
#   Vercel   → { "rewrites": [{ "source": "/(.*)", "destination": "/index.html" }] }
#   Apache   → FallbackResource /index.html

/*    /index.html   200
